<header><h1>Ground Combat: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_ground_combat">Ground Combat</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If ground combat is to happen on multiple planets during a single invasion step, they will be resolved planet by planet, after the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step has been resolved on all planets and before the <b>Establish Control</b> step is resolved on any planet. The active player chooses the order combats are fought in.<sup>3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;Ground combats on multiple planets are resolved in the order of the active player&rsquo;s choice.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The &ldquo;start of combat&rdquo; and &ldquo;start of combat round&rdquo; windows occur before the <b>Roll Dice</b> step.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 42.4a: &ldquo;During the first round of a combat, &lsquo;start of combat&rsquo; and &lsquo;start of combat round&rsquo; effects occur during the same timing window.&rdquo; LRR 42.3: a new round starts &ldquo;with the &lsquo;Roll Dice&rsquo; step.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are &lsquo;start of combat&rsquo; and &lsquo;start of the first combat round&rsquo; abilities in the same timing window, and how often do they happen?&rdquo;: &ldquo;they are the same window, before Anti-Fighter Barrage&rdquo; start-of-combat windows precede combat rolling.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The &ldquo;end of combat&rdquo; and &ldquo;end of combat round&rdquo; windows occur after the <b>Assign Hits</b> step.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 42.4b: &ldquo;During the last round of a combat, &lsquo;end of combat&rsquo; and &lsquo;end of combat round&rsquo; effects occur during the same timing window.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Abilities that trigger &ldquo;at the start of a combat&rdquo;, other than those on agents, can only be resolved during a combat in which the player resolving them is participating.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can abilities that trigger &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; be played in combats you are not participating in? A: No, any non-agent &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; abilities must be played during a combat you are participating in.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may use the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability of a unit involved in a combat, usually a mech, to cancel a hit produced by their opponent.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87: &ldquo;Immediately before a player assigns hits to their units, that player can use the &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability of any of their units.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 78.6a (space combat): &ldquo;Before assigning hits, players may use their units&rsquo; &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; abilities to cancel hits.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>No player may retreat from a ground combat.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR quick reference lists &ldquo;Retreat&rdquo; only under Space Combat.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may score up to one secret objective per ground combat.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 61.7: &ldquo;they can only score one objective during or after each combat.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How and when are action-phase secret objectives scored?&rdquo;: &ldquo;one in a space combat and another in the ground combat that follows is fine.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player only wins a combat if a space combat or ground combat occurred. Destroying all opposing ships with the Space Cannon ability, destroying all opposing ground forces with the Bombardment ability, landing ground forces on a planet without opposing ground forces, or the opposing player avoiding the combat with the <a href="/F_naalu">Naalu</a> player&rsquo;s Foresight faction ability does not count as winning a combat. A planet containing only another player&rsquo;s structures does not cause a ground combat.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Space Cannon, Bombardment or landing on an empty planet count as winning a combat for objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; a combat is a space combat or a ground combat &hellip; Destroying ships with Space Cannon during movement, bombarding away all defenders, or landing unopposed involves no combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The &ldquo;0&rdquo; side of the d10 represents a result of 10.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Are the &lsquo;0&rsquo; faces of the ten-sided dice &hellip; intended to represent the result of a &lsquo;10&rsquo;? A: Yes, the &lsquo;0&rsquo; face is a &lsquo;10&rsquo; result.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the 0 on the ten-sided die count as 0 or 10?&rdquo;: &ldquo;10 &mdash; the Living Rules Reference FAQ confirms the 0 face is a 10.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
